WEBVTT

00:00.760 --> 00:01.720
Mark 5

00:01.720 --> 00:06.900
They came to the other side of the sea, to the country of the Gerasenes.

00:07.680 --> 00:12.240
And when Jesus had stepped out of the boat, immediately there met him out of the tombs

00:12.240 --> 00:14.340
a man with an unclean spirit.

00:15.000 --> 00:19.820
He lived among the tombs, and no one could bind him any more, not even with a chain,

00:20.320 --> 00:25.000
for he had often been bound with shackles and chains, but he wrenched the chains apart,

00:25.300 --> 00:27.060
and he broke the shackles in pieces.

00:27.500 --> 00:29.720
No one had the strength to subdue him.

00:30.600 --> 00:35.820
Night and day among the tombs and on the mountains, he was always crying out and cutting himself

00:35.820 --> 00:36.460
with stones.

00:37.260 --> 00:42.180
And when he saw Jesus from afar, he ran and fell down before him, and crying out with

00:42.180 --> 00:43.500
a loud voice, he said,

00:44.640 --> 00:51.060
What have you to do with me, Jesus, Son of the Most High God?

00:51.760 --> 00:55.920
I adjure you by God did not torment me.

00:56.420 --> 00:58.200
For he was saying to him,

00:59.000 --> 00:59.920
Come out of the manna.

01:00.000 --> 01:01.840
Come out of the manna, you unclean spirit.

01:02.500 --> 01:03.740
And Jesus asked him,

01:04.480 --> 01:06.140
What is your name?

01:06.900 --> 01:07.940
He replied,

01:08.840 --> 01:16.140
My name is Legion, for we are many.

01:17.300 --> 01:20.260
And he begged him earnestly not to send them out of the country.

01:21.120 --> 01:25.860
Now a great herd of pigs was feeding there on the hillside, and they begged him, saying,

01:27.040 --> 01:29.340
Send us to the pigs.

01:30.000 --> 01:31.360
Let us enter them.

01:32.160 --> 01:33.620
So he gave them permission.

01:34.240 --> 01:37.320
And the unclean spirits came out and entered the pigs.

01:37.440 --> 01:42.420
And the herd, numbering about two thousand, rushed down the steep bank into the sea and

01:42.420 --> 01:43.700
were drowned in the sea.

01:44.560 --> 01:47.500
The herdsmen fled and told it in the city and in the country.

01:47.940 --> 01:50.340
And people came to see what it was that had happened.

01:51.060 --> 01:55.960
And they came to Jesus and saw the demon-possessed man, the one who had had the legion, sitting

01:55.960 --> 01:59.360
there, clothed and in his right mind, and they were afraid.

02:00.000 --> 02:04.480
And those who had seen it described to them what had happened to the demon-possessed man

02:04.480 --> 02:05.400
and to the pigs.

02:06.140 --> 02:08.960
And they began to beg Jesus to depart from their region.

02:09.680 --> 02:14.080
As he was getting into the boat, the man who had been possessed with demons begged him

02:14.080 --> 02:15.300
that he might be with him.

02:15.800 --> 02:18.160
And he did not permit him, but said to him,

02:18.960 --> 02:24.820
Go home to your friends and tell them how much the Lord has done for you and how he

02:24.820 --> 02:26.420
has had mercy on you.

02:26.720 --> 02:29.920
And he went away and began to proclaim in the Decapolis,

02:30.000 --> 02:39.100
And when Jesus had crossed again in the boat to the other side, a great crowd gathered

02:39.100 --> 02:41.260
about him, and he was beside the sea.

02:42.300 --> 02:47.520
Then came one of the rulers of the synagogue, Jairus by name, and seeing him, he fell at

02:47.520 --> 02:50.220
his feet and implored him earnestly, saying,

02:51.140 --> 02:53.840
My little daughter is at the point of death.

02:54.880 --> 02:59.880
Come and lay your hands on her, so that she may be made well.

03:00.460 --> 03:06.460
And he went with him, and a great crowd followed him and thronged about him.

03:07.040 --> 03:12.040
And there was a woman who had had a discharge of blood for twelve years, and who had suffered

03:12.040 --> 03:17.660
much under many physicians, and had spent all that she had and was no better, but rather

03:17.660 --> 03:18.400
grew worse.

03:19.400 --> 03:23.600
She had heard the reports about Jesus and came up behind him in the crowd and touched

03:23.600 --> 03:25.440
his garment, for she said,

03:26.260 --> 03:29.980
If I touch even his garments, I will be made well.

03:29.980 --> 03:37.700
And immediately the flow of blood dried up, and she felt in her body that she was healed

03:37.700 --> 03:38.620
of her disease.

03:39.360 --> 03:44.060
And Jesus, perceiving in himself that power had gone out from him, immediately turned

03:44.060 --> 03:45.480
about in the crowd and said,

03:46.120 --> 03:47.700
Who touched my garments?

03:48.620 --> 03:50.240
And his disciples said to him,

03:50.960 --> 03:56.260
You see the crowd pressing around you, and yet you say, Who touched me?

03:56.560 --> 03:59.240
And he looked around to see who had done it.

03:59.240 --> 04:04.400
But the woman, knowing what had happened to her, came in fear and trembling and fell

04:04.400 --> 04:07.060
down before him and told him the whole truth.

04:07.440 --> 04:08.440
And he said to her,

04:09.040 --> 04:12.040
Daughter, your faith has made you well.

04:12.460 --> 04:15.340
Go in peace and be healed of your disease.

04:16.080 --> 04:19.980
While he was still speaking, there came from the ruler's house some who said,

04:20.680 --> 04:22.140
Your daughter is dead.

04:22.800 --> 04:24.560
Why trouble the teacher any further?

04:25.080 --> 04:29.120
But overhearing what they said, Jesus said to the ruler of the synagogue,

04:29.240 --> 04:32.760
Do not fear, only believe.

04:33.560 --> 04:38.200
And he allowed no one to follow him except Peter and James, and John the brother of James.

04:38.640 --> 04:44.080
They came to the house of the ruler of the synagogue, and Jesus saw a commotion, people

04:44.080 --> 04:45.840
weeping and wailing loudly.

04:46.380 --> 04:48.380
And when he had entered, he said to them,

04:48.940 --> 04:52.040
Why are you making a commotion and weeping?

04:52.360 --> 04:54.860
The child is not dead, but sleeping.

04:54.860 --> 04:57.040
And they laughed at him.

04:57.440 --> 04:59.220
But he put them all outside.

04:59.240 --> 05:04.740
And took the child's father and mother, and those who were with him, and went in where the child was.

05:04.740 --> 05:07.240
Taking her by the hand, he said to her,

05:07.740 --> 05:09.740
Talitha, koumi.

05:09.740 --> 05:11.740
Which means,

05:11.740 --> 05:15.740
Little girl, I say to you, arise.

05:15.740 --> 05:20.740
And immediately the girl got up and began walking, for she was twelve years of age,

05:20.740 --> 05:23.740
and they were immediately overcome with amazement.

05:23.740 --> 05:27.240
And he strictly charged them that no one should know this,

05:27.240 --> 05:29.240
and told them to give her something to eat.

